<Column name="QC" id="49AAA22A-49D1-78F4-F9BF-9D1EF61EFA55">
<createdBy>HALAR</createdBy>
<createdTime>2020-07-21 09:14:29 UTC</createdTime>
<comment><![CDATA[Quantity of products contained in the Packaging.
Real number up to 2 digits behind the decimal point, usually an integer.
Rules:
The packages of the trade reference are sorted in ascending order of QC. Ex: BX Box then CT Carton then PF Pallet.
Each package has a different QC value. Example: per box BX: 1 unit, per carton CT: 10 units, per pallet PF: 500 units.
The smallest value of QC is equal to QMV of COMMERCE. MSQ = Minimum Sales Quantity from Distributor to Customer. This is the smallest possible sales quantity.]]></comment>
